      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Don't try to rub the chemical eye drops as this can further irritate the area. Instead, flush your eye immediately with water for 15-30 seconds to try and dilute the solution. If the burning persists, put on a cold compress or store-bought eye drops specifically designed for chemical irritation. You can also consider rinsing the affected eye with milk or a dairy product, as its casein has natural stopping properties, to neutralize the acid. Do not use herbal drops unless the burning has been treated with a flushing rinse.",
